  serving size: 1 serving
---

If you want to serve with @?rice{}(jasmine preferred), start your rice prep now.

== Sauce-Marinade ==

Mix @soy sauce{3%tbsp}(light or all-purpose), @hoisin sauce{1%tbsp}, @rice vinegar{1%tbsp}(or white vine), @chili paste{3%tsp}(Sambal Oelak preferred), and @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp} in a #bowl.

Take out 2tbsp from the sauce mixture and put in a #small bowl{}. Set aside.

To the remaining sauce-marinade, mix in @brown sugar{3%tbsp} and @cornflour/cornstarch{1%tbsp}.

Mix in @chicken stock/broth{3/4%cup}.

== Chicken Prep ==

In the set aside bowl with 2 tbsp of sauce, add @chicken thighs{1.4%lbs}(boneless skinless, cut into 2.5cm / 1" pieces).

Add @ginger{1%tsp}(finely grated) and @garlic{1%tsp}(finely grated) to chicken, mix, then marinate ~{30%minutes}.

== Frying the Chicken ==

Put @cornflour/cornstarch{3/4%cup} on a plate. Piece by piece, roll the chicken in the cornflour. Then, using your hands as a cup, shake so the excess cornflour falls through your fingers.

Heat @oil{} in #deep fryer{} to 350°F. 

In small batches, deep fry the chicken for ~{3-4%minutes}, until golden brown and crispy.

> When chicken is done, it should begin to float. You may need to shake the pieces a bit if they get stuck to see if they are floating.

Drain chicken on a paper towel lined plate.

Preheat #oven to 200°F and move the chicken there to keep warm.

Heat @oil{2%tbsp} in a #large skillet{} over medium heat. Add @garlic{2%cloves}(finely chopped), @ginger{2%tsp}(finely chopped), and @red chilli flakes{2%tsp}. Sauté for ~{30%seconds} until garlic is light golden. 

Add sauce, bring to simmer and stir occasionally until it thickens enough that you can draw a path across pan base, about ~{7-9%minutes}.

Add chicken, tossing to coat quickly.

> The quicker you are, the crispier the chicken stays.

Transfer to serving plate, garnish with @?green onion{}(finely sliced) and @?sesame seeds{}, and serve immediately.